  "body": "These three functions should use` [EnforceRange] long `instead to just `long` to ensure that not valid float values are filtered out and a TypeError is thrown to avoid possible errors (as converting inifinty to zero), check step no. 6 in the [WEBIdl specs](https://heycam.github.io/webidl/#abstract-opdef-converttoint).\r\n\r\nWe have already done something similar in the [offscreencanvas-interface](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/canvas.html#the-offscreencanvas-interface), so it would make sense to change also the [2dContext interface](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/canvas.html#2dcontext). \r\n\r\nSo instead of being\r\n```\r\n  ImageData createImageData(long sw, long sh);\r\n// ...\r\n  ImageData getImageData(long sx, long sy, long sw, long sh);\r\n  void putImageData(ImageData imagedata, long dx, long dy);\r\n  void putImageData(ImageData imagedata, long dx, long dy, long dirtyX, long dirtyY, long dirtyWidth, long dirtyHeight);\r\n```\r\n\r\nit should be\r\n```\r\n  ImageData createImageData([EnforceRange] long sw,  [EnforceRange] long sh);\r\n// ...\r\n  ImageData getImageData([EnforceRange] long sx, [EnforceRange] long sy, long [EnforceRange] sw, long [EnforceRange] sh);\r\n  void putImageData(ImageData imagedata, [EnforceRange] long dx, [EnforceRange] long dy);\r\n  void putImageData(ImageData imagedata, [EnforceRange] long dx, [EnforceRange] long dy, [EnforceRange] long dirtyX, [EnforceRange] long dirtyY, [EnforceRange] longdirtyWidth, [EnforceRange] long dirtyHeight);\r\n```\r\n\r\n@fserb @annevk ",
